<title>FINLAND: NESTE SAYS TO REMAIN ACTIVE CRUDE TRADER.</title>
<headline>NESTE SAYS TO REMAIN ACTIVE CRUDE TRADER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish oil and energy group Neste Oy on Wednesday rejected market talk it was about to pull out of crude oil trading and said it intended to remain an active player in the market.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no way we could concur with the rumour that we are laying off our (trading) staff and pulling out of crude oil trading,&quot; Neste spokeswoman Helena Haapalinna said by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;We still need trading operations and will remain active,&quot; she added. In the near past, Neste has gradually cut back crude trading operations and reduced trading staff &quot;somewhat ... but certainly not substantially,&quot; Haapalinna said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
